---
components: ["SelectableTileGroup", "SelectableTile"]
description: Selectable tiles provide a tile-based interface for choosing multiple options, with built-in keyboard navigation and accessibility.
---

<script>
  import { SelectableTileGroup, SelectableTile } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Group multiple selectable tiles together for multi-selection scenarios.

<SelectableTileGroup legendText="Deployment regions" name="options" selected={["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]}>
  <SelectableTile value="us-east-1">
    US East (N. Virginia)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="us-west-2">
    US West (Oregon)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="eu-central-1">
    EU Central (Frankfurt)
  </SelectableTile>
</SelectableTileGroup>

## Reactive

### One-way binding

Update selected values using the `select` and `deselect` events.

<FileSource src="/framed/SelectableTile/SelectableTileReactiveOneWay" />

### Two-way binding

Bind to `selected` for simpler state management.

<FileSource src="/framed/SelectableTile/SelectableTileReactive" />

## Legend

### Custom content

Use the `legendChildren` slot on `SelectableTileGroup` to provide custom legend content instead of `legendText`.

<SelectableTileGroup name="options-legend-slot" selected={["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]}>
  <strong slot="legendChildren">Deployment regions</strong>
  <SelectableTile value="us-east-1">
    US East (N. Virginia)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="us-west-2">
    US West (Oregon)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="eu-central-1">
    EU Central (Frankfurt)
  </SelectableTile>
</SelectableTileGroup>

### Hidden

Hide the legend visually by setting `hideLegend` to `true`. The legend remains available to screen readers.

<SelectableTileGroup hideLegend legendText="Deployment regions" name="options-hidden-legend" selected={["us-east-1"]}>
  <SelectableTile value="us-east-1">
    US East (N. Virginia)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="us-west-2">
    US West (Oregon)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="eu-central-1">
    EU Central (Frankfurt)
  </SelectableTile>
</SelectableTileGroup>

## Light

Use the light variant for light backgrounds.

<SelectableTileGroup legendText="Deployment regions" name="options-light" selected={["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]}>
  <SelectableTile light value="us-east-1">
    US East (N. Virginia)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile light value="us-west-2">
    US West (Oregon)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile light value="eu-central-1">
    EU Central (Frankfurt)
  </SelectableTile>
</SelectableTileGroup>

## Disabled

Disable specific tiles, or the entire group, to prevent selection.

### Individual tiles

Disable specific tiles to prevent interaction.

<SelectableTileGroup legendText="Deployment regions" name="options-disabled" selected={["us-east-1"]}>
  <SelectableTile value="us-east-1">
    US East (N. Virginia)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile disabled value="us-west-2">
    US West (Oregon)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile disabled value="eu-central-1">
    EU Central (Frankfurt)
  </SelectableTile>
</SelectableTileGroup>

### Entire group

Disable every tile at once by setting `disabled` on `SelectableTileGroup`. This prevents selection natively through the underlying `fieldset`, but doesn't apply the muted disabled tile styling shown above—set `disabled` on each `SelectableTile` too for the visual state.

<SelectableTileGroup legendText="Deployment regions" name="options-disabled-group" selected={["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]} disabled>
  <SelectableTile value="us-east-1">
    US East (N. Virginia)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="us-west-2">
    US West (Oregon)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="eu-central-1">
    EU Central (Frankfurt)
  </SelectableTile>
</SelectableTileGroup>

## Checkmark label

Customize the ARIA label announced for a tile's checkmark icon with `iconDescription`. Defaults to `"Tile checkmark"`.

<SelectableTileGroup legendText="Deployment regions" name="options-checkmark-label" selected={["us-east-1"]}>
  <SelectableTile iconDescription="US East (N. Virginia) selected" value="us-east-1">
    US East (N. Virginia)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="us-west-2">
    US West (Oregon)
  </SelectableTile>
  <SelectableTile value="eu-central-1">
    EU Central (Frankfurt)
  </SelectableTile>
</SelectableTileGroup>
